    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40688" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιπωλέομαι</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>go about, go through</i>, c.acc., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. στίχας ἀνδρῶν</span>, of the general
				<i>inspecting</i> his troops, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				3.196
			</span></i>, etc.; but in <i><span class="en">
				11.264
			</span></i>, of <i>reconnoitring</i> an enemy.—<i><span class="en">
				Them.
			</span></i> has <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιπολεῖσθαι</span></b> 
			<i>visit</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βόσπορον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Or.</u>
					6.75c
				</span></i>
			: c. dat., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σύροις</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				11.152b
			</span></i> (nisi leg. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιπωλ-</span>).</div>
